so let's get this out of the way now no  I'm not that great a call of duty and no  it's not my go to multiplayer game sadly  I can't tell you about the intricate  tweaks made for the latest map designs  for the minor differences in the recall  of an assault rifle what I can tell you  though is that not having really enjoyed  or play the heck out of a Call of Duty  game as much as I did the original  modern warfare I was pleasantly  surprised by advanced warfare the fun it  seems is back in cards but then how  could a game featuring jet packs and  laser-guided smart grenades possibly not  be fun that's why I liked it so much  advanced warfare is as far removed from  the harsh realities of actual war as Cod  has ever been it's futuristic tech may  be based on some real-world visions of  the future but no matter how much it  tries to instill some realism to  proceedings I'm still relief rolling  around in a city strapped to an  exoskeleton it's the stuff sci-fi dreams  and made of most fun for me was the  multiplayer mode uplink here in a  strangely endearing cross between  basketball and classic team deathmatch  your team is tasked with grabbing a  satellite and placing it in the  opposition uplink to score points yes  where we will want all debating the  moral implications of modern warfare  two's no Russian level and being pelted  with Churchill quotes upon death now  we're doing something as daft as having  to slam dunk a satellite ball into a  floating orb of light while trying to  avoid being shot staff though it may be  it is a hell of a lot of fun if someone  grabs the satellite they are marked on  screen causing a mad dash of soldiers  either trying to steal the satellite or  protect the person holding it on smaller  maps like the excellent retreat having  that many soldiers all bunched up in one  place resulting quite a massacre but I  found getting up high and picking off  people amongst the madness worked  wonders for netting if you he kills  getting hold of the satellite was even  better you can't use weapons while it's  in your possession what you can do is  throw the ball around to other members  of your team to take it off even more  fun is throwing the ball to the  opposition which results in an instant  catch giving you ample opportunity to  waste them before picking up the ball  and running off again the other modes I  played hardpoint and Kill Confirmed  didn't have quite the same absurd appeal  as uplink  although Kill Confirmed certainly had  its moments more impressive was the  upgrade system pick 13 which takes its  inspiration from black ops pick 10  mechanic I've always found the upgrade  systems in cob games a little chaotic so  the simplicity of pick 13 is appealing  you're given 13 points to spend on your  avatars loadout and having everything in  one place including upgradeable  scorestreaks  just makes the whole system that much  easier to understand and to tweak loot  drops earned by completing challenges  made the game that little bit sweeter  too sure I might not have been top of  the leaderboard but thanks to loot drops  I still got some cool gear including a  neat warmus recoil free I am are  lightweight rifle that seemed perfect  for those with a less than steady hand  as with a single player sadly we didn't  get any capture of that but there is  supposedly a renewed focus on character  development this time around and one  hopes the inclusion of the mighty Kevin  Spacey has resulted in a deeper  narrative then again what would the  holiday season be without a stream of  brainless one-liners and an unbelievable  amount of clothes shade with a crashing  helicopter but it was the sheer fun of  the multiplayer that really sold  advanced warfare to me  for the first time in a long while I  think I'm actually looking forward to  this year's card
 

